      "writtenOn": "2025-01-16T18:31:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Not sure what is implied by being in sync\n\nSee b/217376291; is that not applicable to Android 16?\n\n\u003e pvmfw is incapable of knowing `new_instance` from instance_hash\n\nAgreed, it should figure it out from `recorded_entry.is_none()`, right?\n\nBut then, why wouldn\u0027t\n```\ninstance_hash !\u003d Some(entry.salt)\n```\nbe an issue as - surely - something has gone wrong since last boot?\n\nI guess my confusion might be coming from the way we\u0027ve changed how CDIs are used between Android 13 (when `new_instance` was required) and now but I\u0027m not sure what change exactly?\n\n\u003e Storing instance-hash in instance.img has no benefit\n\nIf this is true, what\u0027s even the point of `new_instance` nowadays?",
      "parentUuid": "dc4bcfe3_86236d36",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
