      "writtenOn": "2025-01-20T18:29:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Agreed, it should figure it out from recorded_entry.is_none(), right\n\nRight!\n\n\u003e why wouldn\u0027t instance_hash !\u003d Some(entry.salt)\n\nIf we do store salt as the instance_hash - sure it will be the same. My point is that there is no need of storing it. In the past, there was no `instance-id` like identifier so pvmfw would store in in instance.img.\n\n\n\n\u003e I guess my confusion might be coming from the way we\u0027ve changed how CDIs are used between Android 13 (when new_instance was required) and now but I\u0027m not sure what change exactly?\n\n\nNothing much has changed in in case of instance.img based rbp other than the fact the instance-id has replaced the salt. Prior, we needed the storage for salt, now instance-id is stored in host. Both salt/instance-hash are part of hidden input in DICe, so changing those change Microdroid CDIs.\n\n\nMicrodroid continues to need the `new_instance` flag to prevent the mentioned attack (ie, partial reprovisioning in instance.img(Microdroid partition)).",
      "parentUuid": "13aa7c0a_cb6058e7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 49
      },
